mastery.question_text:
Sketch the prism using the given views.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0)--(1.2,2)--cycle;
\node[below] at (1.2,-0.2) {Front / Back};
\draw (3.4,0) rectangle (6.4,2);
\node[below] at (4.9,-0.2) {Side};
\draw (7.4,0) rectangle (9.8,3);
\draw (8.6,0)--(8.6,3);
\node[below] at (8.6,-0.2) {Top};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
Use the triangular front and back views as the two ends. Join matching vertices with parallel edges; the top view's middle line is the ridge.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0)--(1.2,2)--cycle;
\draw (2.4,0)--(4.2,1.1)--(3,3.1)--(1.2,2);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.8,1.1)--(4.2,1.1) (1.8,1.1)--(3,3.1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

